course: dictionary
lesson: 14423
title: Too simple to be true
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An oversimplification is an explanation that makes something far too simple. It leaves out important parts, so the explanation can become wrong or misleading. «Saying the Romans were just cruel is an oversimplification.» The Romans could be cruel, but that one sentence leaves out their roads, their laws and their reasons for going to war.
explain: Ask yourself: what has been left out? Many things have more than one cause. «The bread went mouldy because it was left in the bag.» Is that the whole story? The bag might have been damp, or the kitchen warm. If there is more to it, the first sentence is an oversimplification.
explain: The word can also mean the act of making something too simple. When a friend tells you, «It's easy, just press the red button», and that leaves out the steps that really matter, the friend has made the job sound simpler than it is. Good thinkers notice this and ask, «What's missing?»
fact: An oversimplification is a way of explaining something that makes it far too simple.
fact: It leaves out important parts, so the explanation can become wrong or misleading.
fact: Teachers say «That's an oversimplification» when an answer is too simple to be true.
fact: «A gross oversimplification» means a very big and obvious oversimplification.
fact: Real causes of events are often many, so one simple reason is usually not the whole story.
exercise: Which sentence is an oversimplification? | «Plants need light, water and air to grow, and warmth helps too.» | *«Plants just need sunshine.» | «Some plants grow in deserts.»
exercise: What does oversimplification mean? | A way of making a word shorter | *A way of explaining something that is too simple, so important parts are left out | A picture showing how something works | A very long and detailed explanation
exercise: Mia says, «The war had only one cause.» Her teacher says, «That's a bit of an oversimplification.» Why? | Because teachers never say anything true | Because one cause is always the best answer | Because the war had no causes at all | *Because real causes are often many
test: Ben says, «Dinosaurs died out because it got cold.» His teacher says it is a gross oversimplification. What does that mean? | A joke that makes the class laugh | A long and detailed answer that everyone agrees with | It is a fact that nobody can question | *It is far too simple and leaves out important causes
test: Which sentence is most likely to be an oversimplification? | «Two plus two makes four.» | *«Everything in history happened for just one reason.» | «The Earth goes round the Sun once a year.» | «Water boils at about 100 degrees at sea level.»
exam: Why is «The Vikings were just warriors» an oversimplification? | *It leaves out their traders, farmers and explorers | It has the wrong number of words | It is a fact that is always true | It is too short to be a sentence
